Jove wrote:
>   To a (mere ;^) mortal Gehennom is endlessly terrifying, but not
> boring.  To the regular ascender, it's endlessly boring.  So much
> so that some players will start a new game rather than go through
> it again.
>
>   And that's the way it should be.  Ascension should not be the
> natural outcome of most Nethack games.  An ascension should also
> mean more than that the player has skill in Nethack.  It should
> mean the player spent a lot of time/effort in that game.

I disagree, strongly.  The point of a game is to have fun, and if
you're making a part of it so boring that people are actually quitting
your game, that's a failure.  Especially if they are quitting and
starting up a new character--it's a good sign that the start of your
game is far more fun than the late part, and so maybe the late part
should be improved.

Tedium is not a good thing in a game, and we don't play to grind it out
and show that we can do repetitive chores.



